    "body": "## Summary\n\n`--cuda-graph-backend-prefill breakable` crashes on HIP when decoder SWA bounded replay is on.\n\nCapture dies in `DeepseekV4Model` with `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'late_layer_tail'`. The HIP backend builds `tail_forward_metadata` only on the eager path. The CUDA backend builds a fixed-capacity tail and captures the late layers over it. HIP does not.\n\nOnce that read is guarded, the first live prefill dies in `can_run_prefill_cuda_graph`. HIP borrows the CUDA method, which calls `_prefill_graph_fits_late_tail`. That helper exists only on the CUDA backend.\n\n- Set `tail_forward_metadata = None` in the HIP capture and replay hooks.\n- Treat a missing tail as \"run the late layers on every row,\" in the model forward and in the logits path.\n- Give HIP its own `can_run_prefill_cuda_graph`. It checks the context-length limit only.\n\nEager prefills still use the SWA tail. Graph-run prefills do not, so their late layers run on every row. Contexts past the prefill graph limit, 16384 by default, still run eager.\n\nSeen on MI355, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, TP4, with decoder SWA bounded replay on. With the patch, capture finishes and prefills at or under the limit log `cuda graph: True`.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] Serve DeepSeek V4 on HIP with `--cuda-graph-backend-prefill breakable` and `--enable-decoder-swa-bounded-replay`. Capture should finish.\n- [ ] A prefill at or under the graph context limit should replay. The prefill line shows `cuda graph: True`.\n- [ ] A longer prefill should still run eager.\n- [ ] CUDA is unchanged. The CUDA backend still builds the tail inside the graph.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41623373931](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41623373931)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41623373474](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/4162